split() of a non-string returns nothing, like PICO-8.

Moss Moss resets its palette with apply_pal(G_colorblind and "4:12,3:135"),
i.e. split(false, ","), when colorblind mode is off.  PICO-8 returns nothing
(so all() iterates nothing); z8lua raised "string expected, got boolean".

diff --git a/lpico8lib.c b/lpico8lib.c
--- a/lpico8lib.c
+++ b/lpico8lib.c
@@ -332,7 +332,9 @@
         return 0;
     }
 
-    if (lua_isnil(l, 1)) {
+    /* Like PICO-8, anything but a string or number (nil, booleans,
+       tables) splits to nothing instead of raising an error. */
+    if (!lua_isstring(l, 1)) {
         return 0;
     }
     size_t count = 0, hlen;
